# Run the requests from top to bottom. "Log in" saves the token, and the other requests send it
# as "Authorization: Bearer <token>", like the website does.
# In Docker: http://localhost:8080   Running from Rider: http://localhost:5145
@ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress = http://localhost:8080

### Log in (the account comes from "Seed" in appsettings.Development.json)
POST {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test.planner@via.dk", "password": "Planner123!" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Who am I? (200 with the token, 401 without)
GET {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Wrong password -> 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
POST {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test.planner@via.dk", "password": "wrong" }

### Courses from the database
GET {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/courses
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One course
GET {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/courses/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Rename a course (planners only). Notes are not saved: the Course table has no Notes column.
PATCH {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/courses/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Programming 1",
  "sueCode": "PRO1",
  "notes": null
}

### Import without a file -> 400 FILE_REQUIRED
POST {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/imports
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary--

### Courses without a token -> 401 UNAUTHORIZED
GET {{ExamPlannerServer_HostAddress}}/api/v1/courses
